    {
      "key": "BPHS_TWENTY_SECOND_DECANATE_OF_A_MIXED_PLANET",
      "category": "ayur",
      "source": {
        "text": "BPHS",
        "chapter": "44",
        "verse": "38-39",
        "rank": 1,
        "note": "A mixed planet's decanate as the twenty-second: the body only dries up. The verse sets a mixed planet against a benefic and a malefic without naming one; Mercury and the Moon are read as the mixed pair, being the two the texts turn benefic or malefic by company. Read from the Maharishi Parashara Hora Shastra in R. Santhanam's translation."
