    {
      "key": "BPHS_TWENTY_SECOND_DECANATE_IS_A_SERPENT",
      "category": "ayur",
      "source": {
        "text": "BPHS",
        "chapter": "44",
        "verse": "38-39",
        "rank": 1,
        "note": "A serpent decanate as the twenty-second: the body is eaten by animals and crows. The serpents here are BPHS ch. 44 v. 40's own \u2014 the second and third of Cancer, the first of Scorpio and the last of Pisces \u2014 and not Phaladeepika's, which this chapter's neighbour verse would have no reason to follow; the three texts disagree (crux C98). The twenty-second decanate is twenty-one on from the lagna's, and twenty-one decanates are seven signs exactly, so it falls in the eighth house's sign at the third of it the lagna stands in; its own sign is that eighth counted on by one, five or nine, and its lord is that sign's lord. Read from the Maharishi Parashara Hora Shastra in R. Santhanam's translation."
      },
      "conditions": [
        {
          "type": "or",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "type": "and",
              "conditions": [
                {
                  "type": "planet-in-sign",
                  "planet": 8,
                  "signs": [
                    "CANCER"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "planet-in-degrees",
                  "planet": "LAGNA",
                  "from": 10.0,
                  "to": 20.0
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "and",
              "conditions": [
                {
                  "type": "planet-in-sign",
                  "planet": 8,
                  "signs": [
                    "CANCER"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "planet-in-degrees",
                  "planet": "LAGNA",
                  "from": 20.0,
                  "to": 30.0
